# Flutter-related
**/Flutter/ephemeral/
**/Pods/
# NOTE: macos/Podfile is intentionally COMMITTED (not ignored). The macOS
# target is on Swift Package Manager for most plugins, but `screen_retriever_macos`
# is still CocoaPods-only, so Flutter keeps a Podfile and the Runner project keeps
# its `[CP] Embed Pods Frameworks` phase. On a clean CI checkout the cached
# `.dart_tool` makes `flutter pub get` skip regenerating the Podfile, so without
# the committed file `flutter build macos` reaches Xcode with no Pods integration
# (empty ${PODS_ROOT}) and fails loading the Pods xcfilelists. Committing it (as
# Podfile.lock already is) keeps the macOS release build green. Do not re-ignore
# it until every macOS plugin has adopted SPM.

